/* Brand gradient, lifted verbatim from the octopus mark's own fill
   (public/octopus_oc8.svg's linearGradient stops: cyan -> blue -> purple ->
   pink -> orange) -- applied to every filled `bg-primary` surface app-wide
   (buttons, progress fills, badges, chat bubbles) so the brand's signature
   sweep shows up beyond the mascot itself, not just as a flat Electric Blue.
   Layered on top of the flat `--primary` background-color Tailwind's
   generated `.bg-primary` utility already sets (this rule comes later in
   the cascade at equal specificity, so it wins) -- text/borders/rings stay
   flat (--primary): a 5-stop gradient only reads cleanly on a filled
   surface, not on thin strokes or small type.
   An opacity-modified variant (`bg-primary/90`, used by Button/Badge's
   hover state) changes the now-invisible background-color underneath, not
   this opaque background-image, so it silently loses its visual effect --
   compensated by a brightness bump on hover here instead. */
.bg-primary {
  background-image: linear-gradient(
    135deg,
    #26d9ff 0%,
    #2775ff 20%,
    #7a4dff 45%,
    #e84ba5 75%,
    #ff9a3c 100%
  );
}

